{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The end of all flesh.</b> That I have fixed for them a time of one hundred and twenty years." "<b>Has come before Me.</b> That I have designated for them for repentance." "<b>For the earth is filled with violence because of them.</b> For all of them rob one another. The landowners rob the tenant farmers by force, and the tenant farmers rob the landowners by deceit, so that the earth yields all its produce to the robbers." "<b>And behold, I will destroy them with the earth.</b> I will destroy them together with the earth, for I will destroy the temperament of the earth and the atmosphere through the tilting of the sun's sphere, which shifted from the equality of the day from the Flood onward, as He, blessed be He, explained in His answer to Job (Job 38:4–15). Therefore the lifespans of the human species diminished immediately after the Flood, for the temperaments and the fruits were no longer at their first perfection. And for this reason the human species was permitted to eat living creatures after the Flood."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:23.035297803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}